/**
 * Implementation Guide Publisher
 *
 * If you want to use this inside a FHIR server, and not to access content
 * on a local folder, provide your own implementation of the file fetcher
 *
 * rough sequence of activities:
 *
 *   load the context using the internal validation pack
 *   connect to the terminology service
 *
 *   parse the implementation guide
 *   find all the source files and determine the resource type
 *   load resources in this order:
 *     naming system
 *     code system
 *     value setx
 *     data element?
 *     structure definition
 *     concept map
 *     structure map
 *
 *   validate all source files (including the IG itself)
 *
 *   for each source file:
 *     generate all outputs
 *
 *   generate summary file
 *
 * Documentation: see http://wiki.hl7.org/index.php?title=IG_Publisher_Documentation
 *
 * @author Grahame Grieve
 */

/*
* DONE! Each language will be in a sub-folder \en etc
* DONE! the subfolders will all have the same set of files
* DONE! there will be redirect files in the root that direct based on accept-language
* DONE! pubpack is cloned in the directory
* NA! the only link across directories is in the language picker
* add a marker for multi-lang to the config.json
* if there's no translation for a page, provide the base language page along with an explanation header at the top
* update spec internals to have language list & base target list
* qa.html etc still in the root in english. Point at the default language page for resource issue list
* DONE! - translateable fields in *.json get translated by appending lang directly
* NOT DONE! parse menu.xml and put it in a .po file. generate menu.xml for each language (e.g. menuen.xml)
* templates carry their own translation files
* images copy from root, then copy from lang subfolders
* same deal for assets folders
* packages - one root package, all resources with translations, and subpackages with lowercase tag in package id
* document language alternatives in package-list.json
* Need to provide artifact title translations in the IG resource
* ToC is generated by java, needs to be translated
 */

